Z||000000||speed racer||10-02-2000||10:56 PM||||How much does a used short shifter usaly sell for.||||reg||5
Z||000001||mshill||10-03-2000||12:02 AM||||Seems to me all of the short shifters are used.  They either come out of an 84 or they are cut from a standard one.  Some of the cut ones are going for as much as $40 plus a core charge.  Of course I have one opn ebay right now and the minimum bid is $20 (no bids yet) with one day left. Sorry, no pointer to it at the moment.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Cooter||10-03-2000||12:20 AM||||I bought one from TOM for my 85. When I sold that car and bought the 88, I just made my own because I now have access to a wire welder. I have an original short shifter from an 84- make an offer! When I made my new one, I also cut and extended the cable attachment point further away from the pivit point on the bottom of the shifter. It makes it a little harder to shift, but really cuts the "throw" down a lot more than just the short handle. TOM may still be making/selling them so check with him.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TOM||10-03-2000||01:14 AM||||Yes I have the for $35 no core. The guy selling them for $40 with a core charge used to get them from me. And the Fiero store sells them for $80 and a core charge,||||reg||1
Z||000004||pollock||10-03-2000||12:19 PM||||I bought Rodney Dickman's competition shifter.  Super-short upper stick, and longer lower portion.  Sweet leather boot with new metal hold-down.  about $80... sounds a little pricey, but it looks outstanding.  For what you get, Rodney can't be making much on it.  I recommend it.||||reg||1
